 "notes": "95% CL upper limit on g_agamma from NuSTAR solar observations (axions produced in solar core, reconverted in solar atmospheric magnetic field). Curve traced from the vector paths of Fig. 1 (figures/bound_main_new_data.pdf in the e-print), the blue 'This work' line. Log-axis calibration from tick-label positions (uniform 88.325 pt/decade in mass, 153.69 pt/decade in coupling); vertical offset anchored to the paper's quoted flat limit g_agamma = 7.3e-12 GeV^-1 for m_a <~ 4e-7 eV (label-center calibration independently gives 7.4e-12, <1% difference). Limit is flat at 7.3e-12 from the low-mass end (plotted axis starts at 1e-11 eV; limit is mass-independent below ~2e-7 eV) and rises at higher mass; curve truncated at the plotted axis edge m_a = 1e-3 eV. Not a dark-matter search, so no local DM density assumption or rescaling.",
